description:
### Problem statement
A package defines four mode constants and a module decodes them into four operations: MODE_PASS forwards `a`, MODE_INC adds 1, MODE_DEC subtracts 1, MODE_INV inverts. During a refactor the case arms were reordered and never re-checked against the package, so every mode now performs a neighbor's job. The package is the specification and must not be touched; put the arms back in line with it.

#### Module interface
```systemverilog
package mode_pkg;
    localparam logic [1:0] MODE_PASS = 2'd0;
    localparam logic [1:0] MODE_INC  = 2'd1;
    localparam logic [1:0] MODE_DEC  = 2'd2;
    localparam logic [1:0] MODE_INV  = 2'd3;
endpackage

module pkg_param_mismatch_fix(
    input  logic [3:0] a,
    input  logic [1:0] mode,
    output logic [3:0] y
);
```

#### Requirements
- MODE_PASS drives `y` with `a`, MODE_INC with `a + 1`, MODE_DEC with `a - 1`, MODE_INV with `~a`; all wrap to 4 bits.
- The package constants are the single source of truth; edit only the case arms in the module.
- Keep using the package-scoped names in the case labels rather than falling back to literals.

#### Notes
When the fence and the arms disagree, the fence wins. The failure is quiet because every label is still a legal package constant, so nothing errors: MODE_INC simply forwards, MODE_DEC increments, and two of the four rows still pass by coincidence. Scoping through the package name keeps the linkage visible at the call site.

starter_code:
package mode_pkg;
    localparam logic [1:0] MODE_PASS = 2'd0;
    localparam logic [1:0] MODE_INC  = 2'd1;
    localparam logic [1:0] MODE_DEC  = 2'd2;
    localparam logic [1:0] MODE_INV  = 2'd3;
endpackage

module pkg_param_mismatch_fix(
    input  logic [3:0] a,
    input  logic [1:0] mode,
    output logic [3:0] y
);
    // Arms were rotated during a refactor and never re-checked.
    always_comb begin
        case (mode)
            mode_pkg::MODE_PASS: y = ~a;          // BUG
            mode_pkg::MODE_INC:  y = a;           // BUG
            mode_pkg::MODE_DEC:  y = a + 4'd1;    // BUG
            mode_pkg::MODE_INV:  y = a - 4'd1;    // BUG
        endcase
    end
endmodule

